  "summary_en": "September 2019 French Ministry of Armed Forces AI strategy. It sets guiding principles (trusted, controlled, responsible AI; sovereignty; interoperability) and a roadmap covering ethics committee, data governance, standards, priority areas including robotics and autonomy, organisation, R&D funding and international cooperation. France rejects fully autonomous weapons beyond human control.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Create a permanent ministerial defence ethics committee by end of 2019 with public advisory opinions",
   "France will not develop fully autonomous lethal systems outside human control; command responsibility maintained",
   "Risk analysis from design phase to set 'right level' of trust; mandatory human validation for critical functions",
   "Participate in civil and military AI standardisation and certification (AFNOR, ISO/IEC JTC 1/SC 42)",
   "Establish CCIAD coordination cell and data governance; robotics and autonomy as one of seven priority axes"
